.\" wlan(8) — NextBSD WLAN command-line client.
.\"
.\" NextBSD-original. There is no upstream page to vendor: Apple's equivalent
.\" surface lives inside the closed wifid and is reached via the private
.\" Apple80211 framework (the airport(8) CLI macOS shipped was removed in
.\" Sonoma). This page is written for this tool.
.\"
.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt WLAN 8
.Os NextBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm wlan
.Nd manage 802.11 wireless networks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm scan
.Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm status
.Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm connect Ar ssid
.Op Ar passphrase
.Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm connect Ar ssid
.Fl -eap Cm peap | ttls | tls
.Fl -user Ar name
.Op Fl -password Ar password
.Op Fl -anonymous-identity Ar name
.Op Fl -ttls-inner Cm mschapv2 | pap | chap
.Op Fl -ca-cert Ar path | Li hash://server/sha256/ Ns Ar hex
.Op Fl -server-name Ar name
.Op Fl -no-verify-server
.Op Fl -client-cert Ar path
.Op Fl -private-key Ar path
.Op Fl -key-passphrase Ar passphrase
.Op Ar interface
.Nm
.Cm disconnect
.Op Ar interface
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the command-line client for
.Xr wland 8 ,
the NextBSD 802.11 management daemon.
It scans for networks, joins them, and reports the current association.
.Pp
It is a pure-C Mach client: it looks up the
.Ql org.nextbsd.wlan
Mach service and issues MIG RPCs.
It does not link CoreFoundation or SystemConfiguration, so it is also the
.Em only
supported way for anything above the Mach line \(em including the Gershwin
desktop \(em to drive WLAN.
.Pp
If
.Ar interface
is omitted,
.Nm
acts on the first WLAN interface
.Xr wland 8
owns, which on any single-radio machine is the only one.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "disconnect"
.It Cm list
List the WLAN interfaces
.Xr wland 8
manages.
These are the VAPs it cloned itself, so the answer is authoritative in a way
.Xr ifconfig 8
is not: net80211 VAPs go through
.Fn ether_ifattach
and therefore report
.Dv IFT_ETHER ,
so the media type cannot distinguish
.Li wlan0
from
.Li em0 .
.It Cm scan Op Ar interface
Request a scan and print the results: SSID, BSSID, signal strength, channel,
and security.
.Pp
The scan RPC returns as soon as the scan is
.Em requested ,
not when it completes \(em a full-band sweep takes seconds, and holding a Mach
reply port open that long would be rude.
.Nm
therefore waits for the sweep to finish before reading the cache.
If it has not finished within 15 seconds,
.Nm
prints what is cached, writes a notice to standard error and exits 0.
If the scan fails,
.Nm
says so on standard error and exits 1.
.It Cm status Op Ar interface
Print the current association: state, SSID, BSSID, signal, channel, security.
.Pp
Pay attention to the difference between
.Ql associated
and
.Ql connected .
See
.Sx THE ASSOCIATED / CONNECTED DISTINCTION
below \(em it is the single most confusing thing about 802.11, and it is almost
always the answer to
.Dq it says connected but I have no IP .
.It Cm connect Ar ssid Op Ar passphrase Op Ar interface
Associate with
.Ar ssid .
Omit
.Ar passphrase
for an open network.
.Pp
The network is
.Em remembered
on success \(em stored in a root-owned
.Pa preferences.plist
via SCPreferences \(em so
.Xr wland 8
will autojoin it at the next boot without asking again.
.Pp
Like
.Cm scan ,
this returns once the association has been
.Em requested .
The 4-way handshake takes time; watch it with
.Cm status .
.Pp
.Cm connect
refuses a network the last scan showed as WPA-Enterprise unless
.Fl -eap
is given.
See
.Sx WPA-ENTERPRISE .
.It Cm disconnect Op Ar interface
Disassociate and stop autojoining, until asked again.
.El
.Sh WPA-ENTERPRISE
.Fl -eap
joins a WPA-Enterprise (802.1X) network with PEAP/MSCHAPv2, EAP-TTLS or
EAP-TLS.
Like any other network, it is remembered and autojoined.
.Bl -tag -width "--anonymous-identity"
.It Fl -user Ar name
The identity to authenticate as.
Always required; for EAP-TLS, the name the server expects with the certificate.
.It Fl -password Ar password
The password for PEAP or EAP-TTLS.
If it is absent,
.Nm
reads it without echo from the terminal, or as one line of standard input when
that is not a terminal.
.It Fl -anonymous-identity Ar name
The outer identity sent before the encrypted tunnel starts.
Not sent unless given.
.It Fl -ttls-inner Cm mschapv2 | pap | chap
The inner method for EAP-TTLS.
The default is
.Cm mschapv2 .
.It Fl -ca-cert Ar path | Li hash://server/sha256/ Ns Ar hex
The CA certificate the server's certificate must chain to, as a PEM file, or the
SHA-256 hash of the server's certificate to pin it.
.It Fl -server-name Ar name
The server certificate must carry this name or a name ending in
.Pf . Ar name .
With no
.Fl -ca-cert ,
its chain is checked against the system's roots in
.Pa /etc/ssl/cert.pem .
.It Fl -no-verify-server
Do not verify the server at all.
Anyone advertising the SSID can then collect your credentials.
.It Fl -client-cert Ar path
The client certificate for EAP-TLS, in PEM.
Not needed when
.Fl -private-key
is a PKCS#12 file.
.It Fl -private-key Ar path
The private key for EAP-TLS, in PEM or PKCS#12.
Refused if it is group- or world-readable.
.It Fl -key-passphrase Ar passphrase
The private key's passphrase, if it has one.
.El
.Pp
The server is verified by default.
With none of
.Fl -ca-cert ,
.Fl -server-name
and
.Fl -no-verify-server ,
.Cm connect
fails: there is no one to ask about an unknown server at boot.
.Pp
EAP errors are reported in
.Pa /var/log/wland.stderr .
After a failure,
.Xr wland 8
holds off autojoining enterprise networks; an explicit
.Cm connect
ends the hold.
.Sh THE ASSOCIATED / CONNECTED DISTINCTION
802.11 has two moments that look alike and are not:
.Bl -tag -width "connected"
.It Ql associated
The station has joined the BSS and net80211 has reached RUN state.
.Em The port is not yet keyed .
The interface reports its link UP at this instant, which is exactly why a naive
DHCP client fires a DHCPDISCOVER here and has every packet silently dropped.
.It Ql connected
The WPA 4-way handshake has completed and the port is keyed.
.Em Now
traffic can flow.
.El
.Pp
NextBSD does not guess.
.Xr wland 8
publishes
.Ql State:/Network/Interface/<if>/AirPort
with an
.Ql Authenticated
flag that is true only in the
.Ql connected
state, and
.Xr ipconfigd 8
holds DHCP until it sees it.
So if
.Cm status
says
.Ql associated ,
you have no IP address
.Em on purpose ,
and that is the system working correctly.
If it stays there, authentication is failing \(em nearly always a wrong
passphrase.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/Local/Library/Preferences/SystemConfiguration/org.nextbsd.wland.plist" -compact
.It Pa /var/log/wland.stderr
.Xr wland 8
log.
.It Pa /Local/Library/Preferences/SystemConfiguration/org.nextbsd.wland.plist
Known networks.
.Em Passphrases are stored in plaintext ;
see
.Xr wland 8 .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Find and join a network:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# wlan scan
SSID                             BSSID              SIGNAL   CH SECURITY
Home                             a4:2b:b0:11:22:33  ****  -42   6 WPA2
Cafe                             de:ad:be:ef:00:01  **    -71  36 open

# wlan connect Home hunter2hunter2
associating with 'Home' on wlan0...

# wlan status
interface: wlan0
state:     connected
ssid:      Home
bssid:     a4:2b:b0:11:22:33
signal:    -42 dBm
channel:   6
security:  WPA2
.Ed
.Pp
Watch the handshake complete \(em the moment DHCP is released:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# wlan connect Home hunter2hunter2 && wlan status
state:     associated (not yet keyed)

note: associated but NOT yet keyed \(em DHCP is held until the
4-way handshake completes.

# wlan status
state:     connected
.Ed
.Pp
Join a WPA-Enterprise network, typing the password at the prompt:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# wlan connect Corp --eap peap --user alice \e
    --ca-cert /Local/Library/Corp/ca.pem --server-name radius.corp.example
802.1X password for alice:
associating with 'Corp' on wlan0 (802.1X)...
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -tag -width "wpa_supplicant is not reachable"
.It Sy cannot reach org.nextbsd.wlan
.Xr wland 8
is not running.
Check
.Pa /var/log/wland.stderr
and
.Ql launchctl list | grep wland .
.It Sy no WLAN interfaces
.Xr wland 8
found no 802.11 radio, so it cloned no VAP.
Check
.Ql sysctl net.wlan.devices .
If that is empty, the driver did not attach \(em or, on arm64, net80211 is not
in the kernel at all.
.It Sy wpa_supplicant is not reachable
The interface exists but its
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
died or never started.
.Pa /var/log/wland.stderr
will say why.
.It Sy scan failed
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
reported that the sweep failed.
.Pa /var/log/wland.stderr
has the event.
.It Sy scan did not finish within 15 seconds
No result arrived in time.
The list printed is whatever
.Xr wland 8
had cached.
.It Sy this is a WPA-Enterprise (802.1X) network
.Cm connect
was given no
.Fl -eap
for a network that needs it.
.It Sy server verification needs --ca-cert or --server-name
Give one of them, or
.Fl -no-verify-server
to turn verification off.
.It Sy the private key file is group- or world-readable
Make it readable by its owner only.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr ipconfigd 8 ,
.Xr wland 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
.Pp
.Lk https://pkgdemon.github.io/nextbsd-wlan-plan.html "The NextBSD WLAN plan"
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in NextBSD in 2026.
